 "spin_named": "Caption: 'deng gan' cannon. 登杆 (also written 蹬杆) is cue-sport slang for a punched stun stroke, a firm hit a little above stun so the cue ball checks and then kicks on; my reading of the term, not certain. English subtitles carry commentary only ('he tried...', 'what a shot'), nothing on spin.",
 "spin_inferred": "Hard stun with a little follow (stun run-through), no side visible. The black is hit nearly full (cut about 11 deg) at about 6 m/s. Plain stun would send the cue ball along +19 deg to reach the top cushion near y = +0.16; it reaches it at y = 0.00, so it ran on forward of the stun line. It comes off the top cushion slowly (about 0.9 m/s in, 0.41 m/s once rolling) and square to it (179 deg), about 10 deg more towards +y than a mirror bounce of the straight-line approach; with the approach itself uncertain this says nothing firm about side.",
